You know, that was something
we were like, don't say it yet.

00:01:48.690 --> 00:01:51.860
We're still, you know, the
ink is just getting dry,

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:53.910
everything, et cetera,
et cetera, but yeah,

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:56.100
we can announce that now, and
what it really is, is look,

00:01:56.100 --> 00:01:59.180
when you walk into, and it's
a big thing for me too, right,

00:01:59.180 --> 00:02:00.430
you mentioned a couple of years ago.

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:02.790
Well, a couple of years ago,
I wasn't a father, right?

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:04.290
I didn't have my own kids, right?

00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:06.440
I wasn't looking at life differently.

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:08.190
I was just, it's go, go, go, man.

00:02:08.190 --> 00:02:11.370
Hey, you go back even 10
years, I'm in the Navy.

00:02:11.370 --> 00:02:13.677
I'm deploying, I'm doing
this, I'm doing that.

00:02:13.677 --> 00:02:15.701
You know, I'm not
thinking about that stuff,

00:02:15.701 --> 00:02:16.970
I'm thinking about me, right?

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.590
It's when you're younger, your life

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:19.670
is more centered on yourself.

00:02:19.670 --> 00:02:21.720
That's just how we are,
that's, that's human nature,

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.510
but you know, as you get
older and then when you do

00:02:24.510 --> 00:02:26.040
have kids and you start
thinking more socially,

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.400
being more socially minded,
more broadly minded,

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.926
more, you know, you have
more of a widespread outlook

00:02:30.926 --> 00:02:33.190
on life and you start to
think, well, wait a minute,

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:34.420
what about, what's going on here,

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:35.253
what's going on there?

00:02:35.253 --> 00:02:36.086
How are we doing this,
how are we doing that?

00:02:36.086 --> 00:02:39.400
And when you walk into
one of these, you know,

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:41.670
commercial bookstores
lately, Books-A-Million,

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:44.403
Barnes and Noble, I swear it's
like the first book I see,

00:02:44.403 --> 00:02:46.860
it's always this table that's set out

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.080
and it's children's books
and every single one

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:51.300
of the authors, their last
names is either a Biden,

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:55.100
Obama, Clinton, or a Harris,
right, Meena Harris, the niece,

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:58.280
and so I'm saying, wow, this
is just, it's so politicized

00:02:58.280 --> 00:02:59.160
and I don't remember that.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:01.580
I mean, you know, my
kids' books were like,

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:04.466
the last name was Seuss, it's just basic.

00:03:04.466 --> 00:03:06.556
- You mean that old racist?

00:03:06.556 --> 00:03:07.913
- Right, right, right,
right, right, right.

00:03:07.913 --> 00:03:09.320
You can't even do that.

00:03:09.320 --> 00:03:10.712
I'm learning like "One Fish, Two Fish,"

00:03:10.712 --> 00:03:13.440
and now we're talking
about all of this really

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:17.080
politicized stuff, and so
I said, look, there's been

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:21.395
this idea on the right that,
you know, it was always like,

00:03:21.395 --> 00:03:23.659
it's always like, well, the campus crazies

00:03:23.659 --> 00:03:25.543
will just stay on campus
because then they'll go

00:03:25.543 --> 00:03:28.460
to real life and they'll get
mugged by reality, to use

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:30.562
the old Buckleyan line, and
then they'll stop and they'll

00:03:30.562 --> 00:03:33.460
go back to normal and
everything will be fine, right?

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:34.910
Well, that's not what happened.

00:03:34.910 --> 00:03:38.326
The campus crazies followed
into the corporate crazies,

00:03:38.326 --> 00:03:40.959
the military crazies,
the academia crazies,

00:03:40.959 --> 00:03:42.970
all the crazies, right, everywhere,

00:03:42.970 --> 00:03:45.226
and so, that's now filtering into where?

00:03:45.226 --> 00:03:49.200
Into schools, right, pre-K
through 12, and of course

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:51.490
this is happening with
CRT, et cetera, et cetera,

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:53.410
and the books are a huge part of this.

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:55.830
So the right has been playing this game,

00:03:55.830 --> 00:03:57.675
or not even just the right,
but people who just believe

00:03:57.675 --> 00:04:00.865
in traditional values,
basic American values,

00:04:00.865 --> 00:04:04.480
totally ceded this space,
just totally ceded this space

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.000
and said, oh, it'll correct itself.

00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:07.130
It's self-correcting, don't worry,

00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:08.510
this isn't some big thing.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:09.990
Guess what, folks, it is.

00:04:09.990 --> 00:04:11.920
So, that's why we decided
to put this together.

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:12.780
They reached out to me and they said,

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:14.150
do you wanna do something?

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:16.250
I'm like, I don't know, like,
what should I write about?

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:18.820
And they're like, what's
something that you don't like?

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.104
And I said, communism, right, you know,

00:04:21.104 --> 00:04:21.949
(Dave chuckling)

00:04:21.949 --> 00:04:24.540
and they said, well, it just
so happens that we have a book

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:26.260
that we think that would
lend itself to that.

00:04:26.260 --> 00:04:28.083
So we kinda worked together
on the writing of it,

00:04:28.083 --> 00:04:31.320
and it's actually got,
and this is the one thing

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:33.480
I said to them, I was like
look, I don't wanna do

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:36.500
one of those big preachy
things where it's some story

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:40.143
that all of a sudden, Jack
Posobiec walks over and is like,

00:04:40.143 --> 00:04:42.817
"Well, kids, let's talk
today about the virtues

00:04:42.817 --> 00:04:44.857
"of the free market and Miltonian,

00:04:44.857 --> 00:04:46.880
"Milton Friedman and Ayn Rand."

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:48.040
It like, no, no, no.

00:04:48.040 --> 00:04:50.020
Like, I don't want to
do that stuff, right,

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.540
so they showed me the storyboards on it,

00:04:52.540 --> 00:04:54.120
and I said, this is actually really cool.

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:56.795
Like, this is a book, there's characters.

00:04:56.795 --> 00:04:59.730
They're like, on an island,
there's a marketplace,

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:02.150
but then, you know, some
wolves show up and they say,

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:05.967
hey, come to our island, we've
got free ice cream, you know,

00:05:05.967 --> 00:05:07.170
and this guy is trying to.

00:05:07.170 --> 00:05:09.670
- Not only I'm gonna
illustrate the island here.

00:05:09.670 --> 00:05:11.520
- Oh, you got the post.
- There's a giant.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:13.576
It comes with a big map.
- There's a poster too.

00:05:13.576 --> 00:05:14.820
- I think I got it right here.

00:05:14.820 --> 00:05:16.330
- [Jack] Oh my gosh, yeah, look at this.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:17.580
Right, so the way.

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:20.760
- [Dave] We'll put up a still
so that I'm not so foldy here.

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:22.540
- I know, right.

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:25.702
So the, yeah, so the way it
works is with the whole series

00:05:25.702 --> 00:05:28.040
and there's 12 in the first
saga, there's gonna be

00:05:28.040 --> 00:05:30.330
more sagas of, so it's
like you get one a month,

00:05:30.330 --> 00:05:32.900
and then each one of the
books corresponds with one

00:05:32.900 --> 00:05:35.670
of those circles and the
different places that are

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:37.680
