00:07:08.700 --> 00:07:10.360
of "Star Trek: The Next
Generation," where there's

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:12.373
a replicator and you can
walk over and, you know,

00:07:12.373 --> 00:07:14.360
I've got my Earl Grey tea, right,

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:16.870
but we don't live in that world
and so maybe when somebody,

00:07:16.870 --> 00:07:19.709
and it's just the basic idea,
right, that when someone

00:07:19.709 --> 00:07:22.700
offers you something that seems too good

00:07:22.700 --> 00:07:25.030
to be true, probably is.

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:25.863
- It probably is.

00:07:25.863 --> 00:07:28.170
Now the real question is at the libraries,

00:07:28.170 --> 00:07:31.410
will this book be recommended
by the drag queens

00:07:31.410 --> 00:07:33.380
