00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:37.810
I don't know, maybe while, maybe while

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:39.160
they're getting all the attention,

00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:40.500
we'll just be running around in the back,

00:07:40.500 --> 00:07:42.370
like throwing them all over the place.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:45.040
- So, I mean, I'm super
impressed by this because one of

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:46.690
the things I've been talking
about on the show for a while

00:07:46.690 --> 00:07:50.060
is I, I'm sort of tired
of people that just talk

00:07:50.060 --> 00:07:52.660
and I want to find people
that build and people that do,

00:07:52.660 --> 00:07:55.480
and that's why it's very cool
to me that you were like,

00:07:55.480 --> 00:07:57.986
yeah, I will write a children's
book about these ideas

00:07:57.986 --> 00:08:02.550
because we gotta fix all of
this stuff, but I wanted to read

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:04.670
the, the mission statement by Brave.

00:08:04.670 --> 00:08:05.770
They're the publishers of the book.

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:06.820
I thought this was pretty great.

00:08:06.820 --> 00:08:09.407
"Timeless virtues for a new generation.

00:08:09.407 --> 00:08:12.517
"A progressive agenda is
dominating today's culture

00:08:12.517 --> 00:08:15.077
"and teaching our kids
all the wrong lessons.

00:08:15.077 --> 00:08:17.027
"That's why we created
a book series geared

00:08:17.027 --> 00:08:20.007
